--[[
  A worker runs only where its side runs scripts. The build writes the
  script of `worker.server.actor.aly` as a Script with RunContext
  Legacy, and the script of `worker.client.actor.aly` as a LocalScript.
  So each worker Actor must sit in a container that runs that class:

    Script (RunContext Legacy)   ServerScriptService, Workspace
    LocalScript                  PlayerScripts, PlayerGui, Backpack,
                                 the character, ReplicatedFirst

  The usual mounts do this. `src/server` lands in ServerScriptService.
  `src/client` lands in StarterPlayerScripts, and the engine copies it
  into the PlayerScripts of each player, where the copy runs. A worker in
  `src/shared` lands in ReplicatedStorage, where neither class runs.
]]

import { Pool } from '@packages/foundry'

-- A server pool. A server has no touch screen, so the count is fixed.
-- `worker.server.actor.aly` sits beside this script.
const pool = Pool.start(script.Parent->worker, 4)

print(`{pool:stats().workers} workers on the server`)

--[[
  - The clones go beside the template, so each clone runs where the
    template runs.
  - A worker that never runs never calls `ready`. The pool waits
    `timeout` seconds for a ready worker, then stops, warns, and runs
    each job serial.
  - Rojo makes `.client.luau` a LocalScript. With `emitLegacyScripts =
    false`, it makes a Script with RunContext Client, and such a script
    in StarterPlayerScripts runs twice: as the template and as the copy.
    Keep the default.
  - The server has its own pool, and each client has its own. An actor
    message never crosses the network.
]]
